  "id": "Compound::DB00748 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Carbinoxamine is shown to bind to Cyp2b6 and Cyp2e1, two enzymes involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These enzymes are part of the arachidonic acid monooxygenase and epoxygenase pathways, which are critical for the production of bioactive lipid mediators. The shared participation of Cyp2b6 and Cyp2e1 in these pathways suggests a potential overlap in their functional roles, which may explain the observed interactions between Carbinoxamine and Cyp2d6. The integration of these pathways implies that Carbinoxamine may influence Cyp2d6 through a mechanism involving the modulation of arachidonic acid metabolism. The high scores in the visible paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, supported by the shared participation of these enzymes in the same metabolic processes. This suggests that Carbinoxamine could act as a modulator of Cyp2d6, potentially affecting the metabolic pathways that regulate arachidonic acid conversion. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Carbinoxamine and Cyp2d6, particularly through the influence on arachidonic acid metabolism, which is a recurring theme across the visible paths.",
